:\"ServeMux\"}],\" documentation. Our mount points behave similarly.\"]}],\"\\n\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"\u003ctarget\u003e\"}],\" Serve provides 4 options for serving content: an HTTP reverse proxy, a file, a directory, and static text. A reverse proxy lets you forward requests to a local HTTP web server. Providing a local file path provides the ability to serve files or directories of files. Serving static text is available mostly for debugging purposes and serves a static response.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Reverse proxy\"}]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"To serve as a reverse proxy to a local backend, provide the location of the \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"\u003ctarget\u003e\"}],\" argument. You can write the location to the local service as a port number (for example, \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"3000\"}],\"), a partial URL (for example, \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"localhost:3000\"}],\"), or a full URL including a path (for example, \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"tcp://localhost:3000/foo\"}],\", \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"https+insecure://localhost:3000/foo\"}],\"). Note that only \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"http://127.0.0.1\"}],\" is supported for proxies.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"Example: \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"tailscale serve localhost:3000\"}]]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"Or, to serve over HTTP:\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"Example: \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"tailscale serve --http=80 localhost:3000\"}]]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"HTTP servers are accessible using short MagicDNS names like \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"http://my-node\"}]]}],\"\\n\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"File server\"}]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"Provide a full, absolute path to the file or directory of files you wish to serve. If you specify a directory, this renders a directory listing with links to files and subdirectories.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"Example: \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"tailscale serve /home/alice/blog/index.html\"}]]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"Due to macOS app sandbox limitations, this option only works when using Tailscale's \",[\"$\",\"$L14\",null,{\"href\":\"/docs/concepts/macos-variants\",\"children\":\"open source variant\"}],\". If you've installed Tailscale on macOS through the Mac App Store or as a Standalone variant system extension, you can use Serve to share ports but not files or directories.\"]}],\"\\n\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Static text server\"}]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"Specifying \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"text:\u003cvalue\u003e\"}],\" as a \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"\u003ctarget\u003e\"}],\" configures a static plain-text server.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"Example: \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"children\":\"tailscale serve text:\\\"Hello, world!\\\"\"}]]}],\"\\n\"]}],\"\\n\"]}],\"\\n\"]}],\"\\n\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"$L19\",null,{\"id\":\"use-the-proxy-protocol\",\"children\":\"Use the PROXY protocol\",\"level\":2}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"group relative overflow-hidden\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"absolute right-[5px] top-[21px] flex h-10 w-10 items-center justify-center rounded bg-gray-200 text-gray-1000 opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L18\",null,{\"t